Step 1. Analyze the Mission Description

• The mission requires delivering food from the kitchen to an inpatient room.  
 – There are two delivery methods:  
  ○ Direct table delivery using a special manipulation skill.  
  ○ Tray delivery where the robot places food on its tray and the inpatient (or a helper) retrieves it.  
• The tray method involves uncertainty because some inpatients may be unable to retrieve food and helpers (companion, nurse) might not be available. A query to the inpatient record is needed.  
• In addition, the robot must:  
 – Indicate which meal to retrieve (if tray delivery is used).  
 – Track when and where each meal was retrieved.  
 – Alert if the wrong meal is retrieved.  
• There is also a dish retrieval sub-mission: dirty dishes must be removed from the room. This can be done unassisted or with cooperation (two robots or with human help).  
• Finally, opening the room door is needed and can be performed unassisted or with cooperation (another robot or a human).  
• The mission overall is a composite of food delivery, dish retrieval, and door opening. All three aspects must be completed (AND relationship).

──────────────────────────────
Step 2. Decompose into Goals and Tasks

A high-level goal (G1) is defined to cover the complete room service mission. Its three main sub-goals are:  
 • G1.1: Food Delivery  
 • G1.2: Dish Retrieval  
